      "text": "🌪️ Tropical Cyclone Pentha (Basyang) \n\nTropical Cyclone Pentha, locally known as Basyang, impacted the Philippines, briefly strengthening into a tropical storm before landfall. Its center reached northeastern Mindanao late yesterday, then crossed Mindanao and the Bohol Sea, weakening slightly overnight.\n\n📍 Current status (Fri, 6 Feb | 14:00 PHT)\n• Near Bilar, Bohol\n• Winds 55 km/h (gusts 75 km/h)\n• Moving WNW at 20 km/h\n\n🧭 Forecast\n• Tracking across southern Negros today\n• Entering the Sulu Sea by evening\n• Expected to remain a tropical depression until tomorrow, then weaken further\n• Forward motion likely to slow significantly\n\n⚠️ Main hazards\n💨 Strong winds – gusts up to 70 km/h\n🌧️ Heavy to very heavy rain – 50–100 mm, locally 150+ mm over Cebu, Negros & northern Palawan\n🌊 Flooding and landslides possible, especially in low-lying and urban areas\n\n👉 Stay updated and follow guidance from local authorities.",
